			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates with defensive improvements\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (51f75f11): Centralize sky event emissions via LogSkyEmit for histogram visibility across 7 provider files (LifecyclePhaseState, WorkspaceDelta, DiagnosticProvider, OpenDocument, TerminalProvider, RegisterCommand, RegisterScmProvider). Add defensive URI/path guards: DiagnosticProvider tolerates malformed URIs per entry, PathSecurity.rs rejects empty paths upfront, FileSystem.rs adds empty-path guards for ReadFile/StatFile. Terminal resilience: localPty:createProcess returns explicit error for invalid id, resize clamps cols/rows to minimum 1, resize on disposed terminal returns Null instead of error. Also clarify MarkerDataDTO coordinates are 1-based.\n- Sky (7563ee45): Add defensive error handling to SkyBridge IPC handlers - wrap all Tauri listener handlers, tree-item mapping, TreeView.refresh(), and webview registration in try/catch to prevent one bad handler from crashing the listener loop. Add SSR safety checks for `window` being undefined in GetWorkbench() and GetServices() during Astro's pre-render pass. Isolates failures rather than propagating and breaking unrelated listeners.\n- Cocoon, Output, Rest: Submodule sync to latest.\n\nBrings defensive hardening across the Element umbrella improving resilience during startup, view transitions, and extension host reloads.",
			"SHA": "d1fcac150f8bd483c8f4ccc0b816095229ef2401"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:52:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates completing extensions race fix\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (2b89f60a): Fix boot-time extensions race and add missing getLatency handler. Add polling to extensions:getInstalled to resolve race condition where workbench caches empty extension list before ExtensionPopulate completes its scan (~250-500ms). Poll ScannedExtensions map for up to 3 seconds before returning empty, ensuring 113+ extension contributions appear in activity bar. Also add localPty:getLatency handler returning empty array per VS Code's IPtyHostLatencyMeasurement[] contract, eliminating \"Unknown IPC command\" log noise.\n- Output (1f47ba96): Correct ViewContainersRegistry registry ID in ViewRegistrySnapshot diagnostic. The function was using guessed ID 'workbench.view.containersRegistry' which returned null. Fix uses correct stock VS Code registry ID 'workbench.registry.view.containers' from vs/workbench/common/views.ts, enabling SkyBridge diagnostics to correctly report extension view counts.\n- Cocoon (92c434cd): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nThis synchronization completes the extensions race fix cycle and restores diagnostic visibility for extension view registration.",
			"SHA": "7cb6fd54f7e6dbacaf3b2080992789658f0ca3ca"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:38:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates across Element fleet\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Mountain (c661d669): Fix duplicate DevTools window in debug builds where WindowBuild.rs and AppLifecycle.rs were both calling open_devtools(). Remove the redundant call and document that DevTools auto-open lives in AppLifecycle. Also clarify DiagnosticProvider docstring specifying 1-based indexing for StartLineNumber/StartColumn/EndLineNumber/EndColumn.\n\n- Output (8990969b): Disable PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration transform from default build pipeline. The transform fixed WebGL atlas font glitches but introduced \"black shadow over text\" artifacts in WKWebView's DOM renderer. Keep file on disk for potential re-enablement. Also add ViewRegistrySnapshot() to __CEL_SERVICES__ facade for diagnostic probing of extension view registration.\n\n- Sky (876ea919): Add reentrancy guard to InstallSkyBridge (_SkyBridgeInstalled, _SkyBridgeInstallPromise) to prevent duplicate Tauri listen() registrations on view-transitions, webview reloads, and dev HMR. This fixes the \"workbench loading twice\" / \"purple overlays\" double-render bug. Add phase advancement script to Layout.astro before workbench import. Update astro.config.ts: set output=\"static\", disable clientPrerender/contentIntellisense, add queuedRendering config.\n\n- Cocoon (9b9f7fa): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nBrings cross-cutting synchronizations including reentrancy fix, diagnostic improvements, and terminal pipeline adjustments across the Element umbrella.",
			"SHA": "caa2b47f1191fb5434a7e50db4b37bd50065cafa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:43:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates completing terminal race fix\n\nSynchronize Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (c2d0beca): Complete the terminal race-condition fix by deferring the `sky://terminal/create` event with a 120ms delay. This addresses the timing vulnerability where the Tauri event arrived before `_ptys.set(id, pty)` completed during step 1 (RPC in-flight), causing `_ptys.get(id)` to return undefined and silently dropping keystrokes. Complements the earlier fix in c99ccbe that added the `AppendTerminalOutput` replay buffer for data events.\n- Output (8d7a19d): Add disabled `PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration` transform that defaults `terminal.integrated.gpuAcceleration` to `'off'` to work around xterm.js WebGL texture atlas font drift in WKWebView. Available on-disk for re-enabling if needed.\n- Cocoon (4336123): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nThis synchronization completes the terminal race-condition fix cycle that began with bf94e30, restoring proper terminal panel functionality.",
			"SHA": "8e808838d772556db83ca0d4bd0d22c2dde6ada1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:20:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Return integer id from localPty:createProcess\n\nSynchronize Mountain to c99ccbe7 which fixes the blank terminal panels issue. The VS Code terminal workbench expects `IPtyService.createProcess` to return a `Promise<number>` (the integer terminal id), but Mountain was returning the full `{id, name, pid}` object. This caused the workbench to key its internal `_ptys` map incorrectly, making `_ptys.get(<integer>)` lookups return `undefined` from `onProcessData`/`onProcessReady`, resulting in xterm receiving zero bytes despite Mountain's PTY reader emitting data continuously.\n\nThe fix splits the terminal handler into three distinct paths: spawn preserves full response for Cocoon's Sky bridge, createProcess returns only the integer id per VS Code contract, and start is a no-op for the eager-spawn pattern.\n\nAlso sync Cocoon submodule to 15690303.",
			"SHA": "bf94e30b447208b59dc62d5ad0d591a239a6a530"
		}
	],
